Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: retain the transmit control flags parameter

Backports 7.2 passes control flags through the 802.3 transmit path. The NSS
simple-transmit patch also adds that parameter; retain it instead of shadowing
it with the older local variable. Queue selection may update these flags.

--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -4998,7 +4998,6 @@
 	struct sk_buff *seg, *next;
 	unsigned int skbs = 0, len = 0;
 	u32 priority = skb->priority;
-	u32 ctrl_flags = 0;
 	u16 queue;
 	unsigned char *ra = ehdr->h_dest;
 	bool multicast;
